NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const MODIFIER_ALIASES: Record<string, CanonicalModifier | \"Mod\">;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/constants.ts#L61","children":[{"type":"text","value":"constants.ts:61"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maps modifier key aliases to their canonical form or platform-adaptive 'Mod'."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This map allows users to write hotkeys using various aliases (e.g., 'Ctrl', 'Cmd', 'Option')\nwhich are then normalized to canonical names ('Control', 'Meta', 'Alt') or the\nplatform-adaptive 'Mod' token."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The 'Mod' and 'CommandOrControl' aliases are resolved at runtime via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveModifier()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nbased on the detected platform (Command on Mac, Control elsewhere)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"remarks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remarks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Case-insensitive lookups are supported via lowercase variants"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"MODIFIER_ALIASES['Ctrl'] // 'Control'\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Cmd'] // 'Meta'\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Mod'] // 'Mod' (resolved at runtime)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"remarks","text":"Remarks","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst MODIFIER_ALIASES: Record<string, CanonicalModifier | \"Mod\">;\n```\n\nDefined in: [constants.ts:61](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/constants.ts#L61)\n\nMaps modifier key aliases to their canonical form or platform-adaptive 'Mod'.\n\nThis map allows users to write hotkeys using various aliases (e.g., 'Ctrl', 'Cmd', 'Option')\nwhich are then normalized to canonical names ('Control', 'Meta', 'Alt') or the\nplatform-adaptive 'Mod' token.\n\nThe 'Mod' and 'CommandOrControl' aliases are resolved at runtime via `resolveModifier()`\nbased on the detected platform (Command on Mac, Control elsewhere).\n\n## Remarks\n\nCase-insensitive lookups are supported via lowercase variants\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Ctrl'] // 'Control'\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Cmd'] // 'Meta'\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Mod'] // 'Mod' (resolved at runtime)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: MODIFIER_ALIASES\ntitle: MODIFIER_ALIASES\n---\n\n```ts\nconst MODIFIER_ALIASES: Record<string, CanonicalModifier | \"Mod\">;\n```\n\nDefined in: [constants.ts:61](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/constants.ts#L61)\n\nMaps modifier key aliases to their canonical form or platform-adaptive 'Mod'.\n\nThis map allows users to write hotkeys using various aliases (e.g., 'Ctrl', 'Cmd', 'Option')\nwhich are then normalized to canonical names ('Control', 'Meta', 'Alt') or the\nplatform-adaptive 'Mod' token.\n\nThe 'Mod' and 'CommandOrControl' aliases are resolved at runtime via `resolveModifier()`\nbased on the detected platform (Command on Mac, Control elsewhere).\n\n## Remarks\n\nCase-insensitive lookups are supported via lowercase variants\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Ctrl'] // 'Control'\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Cmd'] // 'Meta'\nMODIFIER_ALIASES['Mod'] // 'Mod' (resolved at runtime)\n```\n"}
